fluxecho.module.eco_dome=Eco Dome
tile.fluxecho.module_core.eco_dome.name=Eco Dome Core
fluxecho.eco_dome.tip=§3The Flux Nexus's greenhouse§r\nA glass dome with floating garden islands round a tree of light\nTwelve planters keep the team's bee, sapling, seed and butterfly samples; it works while docked on its nexus and powered from the team wireless network
fluxecho.eco_dome.structure=§bThe Eco Dome: a glass dome 27×35 and 21 high§r\n· The nexus's construction raises it on a hall site (to the nexus's right first, then its left, then behind it): once the Eco Dome is researched the nexus projects it, and with the materials supplied it builds itself block by block\n· A portal block before a glazed drum and dome; inside, a gallery, two floating islands and a world tree of light\n· 12 planters of 3 Sample Sockets each, 36 samples; a planter is used as a whole: right-click any part of it holding a sample to plant it, empty-handed to open the dome; sneak-click a socket empty-handed to take its sample back\n· The core in the portal between the two doors, two blocks above the foundation, facing the nexus\n· Made of Module Foundation and frame parts, Campus Deck and Wall Panels, Steel Glaze, Basin Rims, Sample Sockets and Cladding Anchors (NEI shows it in 3D with its materials)\nStructureLib's hologram projector previews and builds it
